## 15. AI error detection and repair

The platform should automatically detect:

- Missing images.
- Broken links.
- JavaScript errors.
- CSS layout problems.
- Mobile overflow.
- Missing components.
- Build failures.
- Accessibility problems.

Example interface:

SaipratapS❤️C Website Check

2 warnings

Mobile navigation overflow

Missing image alternative text

HTML validation passed

Build successful

Required behavior: AI Fix button automatically repairs detected issues

AI repair workflow:

1. Detect error.
2. Explain error.
3. Generate correction.
4. Apply correction.
5. Rebuild project.
6. Run tests again.
7. Display updated preview.

Limit automatic repair attempts to prevent excessive AI usage.

## 16. Website testing engine

Before publishing, test:

| Test            | Expected result            |
| --------------- | -------------------------- |
| HTML validation | Valid markup               |
| Build test      | Successful build           |
| Mobile test     | Responsive layout          |
| Link test       | No broken internal links   |
| Asset test      | Images and assets load     |
| JavaScript test | No critical runtime errors |
| Accessibility   | Basic accessibility checks |
| SEO             | Metadata validation        |
| Security        | Basic security checks      |

Only deployment-blocking errors should prevent publishing. Non-critical warnings should be displayed without unnecessarily blocking publication.

